  "local05Dispositions": [
    {
      "id": "AC5-L05-01",
      "verdict": "AGREE",
      "reason": "The repaired X25 separates the single-field Burning Hands/self-dispel fixture from the mutually suppressing two-field fixture. In fixture A, A is wholly outside F1, B intersects F1, W1's 15-foot cone legally reaches both, and no contradictory F2 exists. In fixture B, radius-10 fields centered 8 feet apart genuinely cover each other's application loci, so the immutable Greater Dispel operation snapshot produces the stated mutual suppression without the prior impossible 15-foot coverage claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5-L05-02",
      "verdict": "AGREE",
      "reason": "The repaired X12 uses the actual radius-10 sphere centered at (-1,0,5) and records real sphere/panel intersections. The six central 2.5-foot panels spanning y[-2.5,+2.5], z[0,7.5] are wholly inside the sphere and provide a legal 5-by-7.5-foot opening for the stated 6-foot-tall Medium body; additional clear suppressed portions resume separately. The rule no longer treats the sphere as a rectangular six-panel suppressor."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC5-L05-03",
      "verdict": "AGREE",
      "reason": "The portal movement precision matches COMBAT_ACTION_PLAYTEST.md: use strongest terrain rate 1/2/3 per foot, then add +1 for crawling and +1 for squeezing. Therefore a 5-foot difficult+squeeze traversal costs 15 feet and difficult+crawl+squeeze costs 20 feet. The candidate correctly replaces multiplier language without altering the accepted movement system."
    }
  ],
